! Second-order basis functions with a p-multigrid preconditioner, smoothed by
! the composite complex smoother "cjacobi+isgs": a complex Jacobi sweep over the
! owned-rows matrix, then InternalComplexSGS over the local vectors, which skips
! the interface rows a Gauss-Seidel cannot update without communication, then a
! closing Jacobi sweep that carries the interior's improvement out to those rows
! and exchanges them again. This is the csgs setup of
! VectorHelmholtzWaveguideCsgs with the smoother swapped, so the two share a
! reference norm.
!
! The composite is the complex smoother meant for several partitions. "icsgs" on
! its own is only its second half: it leaves the interface rows unsmoothed and
! never exchanges them, so it is not a standalone parallel smoother by design.
! Note that the composite weakens as partitions are added, since more rows fall
! on an interface and only the Jacobi sweeps reach those: the residual reduction
! per sweep on this mesh runs 0.37, 0.73, 0.79, 0.99 at one, two, three and four
! partitions and exceeds one by six, where it stops being a contraction at all.
! That is the nature of the smoother rather than a defect -- the blocks it
! relaxes exactly are the partition interiors, so more of them means a weaker
! preconditioner -- but it is why the task counts here stay modest. Four is left
! out as too close to the edge to gate on.

  Use Piola Transform = True
  Quadratic Approximation = True
  Gradient Basis Functions = True

! Outer iteration
  Linear System Solver = iterative
  Linear System Iterative Method = GCR
  Linear System Max Iterations = 100
  Linear System GCR Restart = 50
  Linear System Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-7
  Linear System Residual Output = 1
  Linear System Scaling = True

  Linear System Preconditioning = multigrid

! MG parameters only active when preconditioning is set as "multigrid"
  Edge Basis = True
  MG Method = p
  MG Levels = 2
  MG Max Iterations = 1
  MG Smoother = cjacobi+isgs
  MG Pre Smoothing iterations = 6
  MG Post Smoothing Iterations = 6
  MG Smoother Relaxation Factor = $ 1/6

  MG Lowest Linear Solver = Direct
  mglowest: Linear System Scaling = True
  mglowest: Linear System Direct Method = umfpack

! The reference norm is inherited from the serial cjacobi variant, so the norm
! has to be counted the same way when the case is run on several partitions.
  Nonlinear System Consistent Norm = True
